142 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (Following an extensive redesign, the Chassis team has moved into full manufacturing. Over the past year, the team researched the optimal weight, material, and geometry for the frame, validated the design through material analysis and finite element analysis \(FEA\), and completed the full chassis model in SolidWorks. In parallel, a dedicated aerodynamics subteam is researching aero concepts and vehicle setups to prepare for practical testing once the car is complete.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
143 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (This semester, the Powertrain team focused on building the foundation of the car's drivetrain and packaging architecture, prioritizing reliability, serviceability, and performance while staying compatible with the new chassis. Working closely with the Chassis and Drivetrain groups, the team refined the CAD model of the engine placement, engine mounts, and differential mounts. Modeling these components early let them catch interference zones, confirm chain line alignment, and optimize the car's overall mass distribution before any parts were manufactured.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
144 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (The Electrical team has identified every component and connection in the car's electrical system, including wiring, connectors, fuses, relays, the display, and driver controls. They built a detailed spreadsheet mapping each connection and wire run, which ensures the correct wire gauges and connectors are ordered the first time. The team is now developing the computer-based wiring harness design in preparation for fabrication.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
